From d0cc66e9f4db4644492881e129f185584f8c0d44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:08:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): kanban_create refuses a second owner for work
 an open card already does [daveey]

A chat counted Stage B owners by its own chat links (only finished Stage A cards), found none, and created
"Stage B" on the default board while Stage B ran on board research-x from another chat. Nothing in
kanban_create looked beyond an identical retry or an idempotency key.

hermes_cli/kanban_overlap.py scans open cards on every board of this gateway (live board DBs) and on every
other gateway (the hermes-hub replica, hub.db) BEFORE placement routes the card away. A card matches when the
new card names its board (title slug, or /<slug> / "board <slug>" in the body, e.g. a example-org/<slug> repo)
and the titles share a word, or when the titles share >= half of the longer title's significant words (3+).
Parents, the creator's own card, and cards the same chat/worker created are never matches; closed cards never
match; a missing replica is skipped and logged, never a block. On a match nothing is created and the result is
code=create_overlap with the cards (id, gateway, board, status, linked chats). distinct_from + distinct_reason
overrides; every refusal/override writes a create_overlap event (the coach's create_overlap_watch counts
overrides later archived as duplicates). kanban.create_overlap_check: false turns it off.

Offsets: _runs_where and the marker-placement result fields move to tools/kanban_tools_placement.py.
tests/conftest.py points HERMES_HUB_STATE at a per-test dir so the host's live hub replica never leaks in.
Self-heal agent-e1f3f31a01.
